       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day. That is more than twice the usual maximum of 4,000 mg/day for adults, and many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day. A dose that high carries a serious risk of acute liver injury, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily**, which is 3,000 mg/day.\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours**, which is 2,600 mg/day.\n- **3,000 mg/day total**, divided another way.\n\nIf 3000 mg per dose is what you want, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that it's intentional. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
