       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 9,000 mg/day is a toxic dose. It could cause severe liver injury or liver failure, and I can't find a clinical scenario where it would help this patient. Normal liver function and a weight of 70 kg don't lower that risk. A single 3,000 mg dose is already well within the range where you'd want to follow the maximum daily limit.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- Enter a standard dose right now, such as 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day) or 650 mg PO every 6 hours.\n- Enter 3000 mg as a single dose, if that was what you meant.\n- Help you reach pharmacy or a clinical decision support team if you think there's an unusual indication I don't know about. They can review it and enter it through a formal override.\n\nIf this was a typo, such as 1000 mg instead of 3000 mg, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it."
